                <pb facs="0597" n="487" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg487"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/5551: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-04-12T11:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 12,
                                1928—11 a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>92. Your telegram No. 173, April 11 [<hi rendition="#italic">10</hi>], 5 p.m. The
                    Department does not feel that you should make any representations or comment in
                    any way on the action of President Diaz. We prefer not to have anything to do
                    with the candidates, platforms, or issues in this campaign.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
